*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This is not a difficult level. The principal strategy is stopping THE SLOTH and chipping it down using [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|area attackers]], like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Figure Skating Cats]] or [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]]. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] can also be helpful if you use THE SLOTH's slow attack rate to your advantage.

However it could take a long time to beat if your units aren't high leveled. You would know you are winning if THE SLOTH is not advancing to your base. Be patient or bring a [[Battle Items|speed up]].

On 4 crown difficulty, you will want Cyborg Cats to chip down THE SLOTH since at 600% magnification it grows to ''1.8 million HP'' and ''48,000 damage per hit'', one or two-shotting anything that stands in its range of 450. a Lv.40 Awakened Bahamut Cat can deal up to 500,000 damage when timed between THE SLOTH's attacks, although his cooldown only gives the opportunity to pull this off once or twice at most. Just spam meatshields and Cyborgs (the peon waves will give you money) and  THE SLOTH will eventually go down.

